\end{aligned}$$ We expand each of the terms $(x\pm 1)^{2l}$ into its binomial series, i.e., $$(x+1)^{2l} = \sum_{k=0}^{2l} b_{2l,k} x^{2l-k} 1^k \quad \text{and} \,\, (x-1)^{2l} = \sum_{k=0}^{2l} b_{2l,k} x^{2l-k} (-1)^k, \quad
