## Extended phase

Let us consider the case $V_0<J$. In this regime numerical results show that all eigenstates of $\hat{H}$ in real space are extended and the energy spectrum is entirely real (unbroken $\mathcal{PT}$ phase), filling the interval $(-2J,2J)$. Here we provide a rigorous proof of such results. Let us consider the Hamiltonian $\hat{H}_1$ in momentum space \[Eq.(6)\]. For an arbitrary integer $n_0$, a formal solution to Eq.(6) is given by $$\phi_n \propto \left\{
\begin{array}{cc}
0 & n <n_0 \\
1  & n=n_0 \\
\frac{V_0}{E-W_n} \phi_{n-1} & n >n_0
\end{array}
\right.$$ with energy $E=W_{n_0}=2J \cos(2 \pi \alpha n_0)$. Such a solution is an eigenstate of $\hat{H}_1$ provided that $|\phi_n|$ does not diverge as $n \rightarrow \infty$. In particular, if $\phi_n \rightarrow 0$ as $n \rightarrow \infty$ and $\sum_n |\phi_n|^2 < \infty$, the eigenstate is localized. The localization properties of the solution (9) are derived by computing the Lyapunov exponent

