Eq. <a href="#seq" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="seq">[seq]</a> constitutes a linear system of equations for $\alpha_n$. The eigenenergy, i.e., $E$, corresponds to the zero determinant of the coefficient matrix. It is noted that the degree of freedom of bath has been eliminated in the above derivation. For clarity, in the following discussion, Eq. <a href="#seq" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="seq">[seq]</a> is referred as the reduced Schrödinger equation of the system, and $E$ is referred as the reduced eigenenergy of system. The integral, i.e., $$\begin{aligned}
