### Multifractal states

The multifractal nature of a quantum state can not be ascertained from the IPR alone. To this end, we now present computation of a generalized IPR defined as $$\begin{aligned}
I_m^{(q)} &=& \sum_{j=1}^L|\psi_m(j)|^{2 q} \label{mfrac}
\end{aligned}$$ where $I_m \equiv I_m^{(2)}$. It is well-known that $I_m^{(q)} \sim
L^{-\tau_q}$, where the fractal dimension of the state is given by $D_q= \tau_q/(q-1)$. We note that for delocalized states $D_q=1$ for all $q$, while for localized states $D_q=\tau_q=0$. Multifractal states typically yield $0<D_q<1$.

