Of course, the vast scenario o WW phase-space QM is not constrained by the short set of the above properties as it also depicts the probabilistic interpretation from Schrödiger picture of QM, providing the tools for connecting averaged values with quantum observables as well as admitting extensions from pure states to statistical mixtures[^2].

From a broader perspective , the WW picture encompasses scenarios since from plasma and nuclear physics up to quantum chaos and quantum cosmology , including, for instance, the investigation of scattering and decoherence in the context of semiconductor transport process phenomenology . It has also been considered in the interpretation the wave-function collapse problem , in the paradigmatic extension of the standard QM , and as a background for parallel frameworks which include Husimi $Q$ and Glauber-Sudarshan representations of QM, and the highly specific optical tomographic probability framework .

